    tldr: "NordICC, the first randomised trial of colonoscopy screening, invited 84,585 people aged 55 to 64 to a single colonoscopy or to no screening. Bowel cancer incidence fell 18% over ten years among those invited, but only 42% attended, and the fall in bowel cancer deaths did not reach statistical significance, fuelling debate over colonoscopy versus stool-test programmes.",
